[FATAL] TOO MANY STEPS (NULL char) state ('0x563ea3664520' type 16 initial type 6 current 0x563ea3666960 current_type 6 index 0)  in alabnf_matcher.c alabnf_matcher_resolve_state_node 835

__________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

state

initial node vs current node.

ALABNF_NT_SEQUENCE

initial node keep fact we are in a sequence

next_sequence is used to keep track of this sequence step, current node is node of next_sequence
when next_sequence == initial node sequence => start
when next_sequence is NULL => end of sequence.

current node will move from first node to last node of chained sequence.
when current node is consumed it is set to NULL.

initial == current
next_sequence = sequence(initial)
current = next_sequence.node

==> call with current != initial
==> means current is current ... don't care it is part of a sequence.
special case if current is SEQ => need to push a new state.
current node is set to NULL, meaning we have to use next_sequence to progress.




